        "original_id": "831ea86b-11e6-5ffd-846d-3fd3a7c6a033",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tressie Souders, Padmarajan\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, author\n- Works: A Woman's Error\n- Topics: African American women in film, Malayalam literature, Malayalam cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Tressie Souders was born on February 7, 1897, and died on January 17, 1995.\n- In 1922, Tressie Souders directed the feature film \"A Woman's Error.\"\n- Tressie Souders was the first known African American woman to direct a feature film.\n- Padmarajan, also known as Padmarajan Pillai, was born on May 23, 1945, and died on January 24, 1991.\n- Padmarajan was an Indian author, screenwriter, and film director.\n- Padmarajan was known for landmark works in Malayalam literature and Malayalam cinema.",
